Z||000002||Racer 1||12-22-1999||03:29 AM||||A fiero is only as dangerous as its driver. Unless you get the "year" fiero that might catch on fire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">. Those are the fun ones to own kinda risky like james bonde.||||reg||3
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||12-22-1999||03:30 AM||||I agree with you Overlord, most of the people who tell me about my own car have never driven a Fiero and that just sets me off! It never ceases to amaze me how much ignorance is blindly accepted as fact out there concerning the Fiero. The technology that makes the Saturn one of the safest car on the market started with the Fiero. Its offers more protection for the occupants of the car than any other car in its class. The other "dangerous" story is the fires in 84 (and only in 84). Out of the 100,000+ Fieros made in 84, .004% of those cars reported to have a fire that destroyed them. If you didn't take care of the oil levels the engine would do very nasty things like punch a hole through the block with a con rod. Something any engine might do if low on oil. All of these problems were answered except the fix to repair a ruined reputation. <BR>Beware of these people who tell you these stories, usually its "what they heard." I really love it when these non-Fiero people then try to tell long time Fiero owners the same stories as if they are in the position of expertise. They only exhibit their own ignorance. <BR>Sorry for the rant but it just really annoys me when these people try and tell me whats wrong with my Fiero. Thanks Call for coming to this site to find the truth, it would seem that many people blindly accept hearsay as fact without even asking questions. Also might I say again that this is best and friendliest place for the truth about the Fiero. ||||reg||9
Z||000004||Dan||12-22-1999||06:04 AM||||Check this out:http://members.aol.com/topfiero/fiero.txt||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||09:33 AM||||Go, WKDFIRO!!  That's exactly right.  Look inside a Fiero door sometime.  It has 2 big bars for side impact protection.  Isn't it amazing that it's only been in the last few years that anyone has cared about that, but a car that has been discontinued for almost 12 years had it from the start?  And did you know that the **ONLY** car in the '80s to better the Fiero in safety was the Volvo.  Volvo has always been at the top of the safety list.  Don't let anyone lie to you and let me say this again.  The **ONLY** car in the '80s to better the Fiero in safety was the Volvo.  If anyone tells you that Fieros are unsafe, look in their eyes and see if they're brown.  If so, it might be because they're full of sh**!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
